@bio:

Jesse Rodin is the Osgood Hooker Professor of Fine Arts at
Stanford University and a Guggenheim Fellow. He directs the
vocal ensemble Cut Circle (cutcircle.org) and the <i>Josquin
Research Project</i> (josquin.stanford.edu) and co-directs
<i>Mapping the Musical Renaissance</i> (renaissancemapping.org).
His most recent book (Cambridge University Press, 2025) is
titled <a href="https://www.cambridge.org/us/universitypress/subjects/music/medieval-and-renaissance-music/art-counterpoint-du-fay-josquin?format=HB"><i>The Art of Counterpoint from Du Fay to Josquin</i></a>. This
past spring Cut Circle released <a href="https://cutcircle.org/recordings/josquin-ii/"><i>Josquin: II. Missa L’ami
Baudichon; Milanese Motets</i></a>, the second installment in a
cycle of thirteen recordings devoted to Josquin’s
complete works.


@@END: BIO